# What `railway up` must not send to the builder.
#
# `up` uploads the working directory, which on a developer machine holds roughly 900 MB of build
# output — a 446 MB node_modules, a 215 MB virtualenv, and two Next.js build directories. None of
# it is an input to the image: the Dockerfile installs its own dependencies from lockfiles, so
# shipping these only slows the upload and risks the builder running out of room.
#
# Kept separate from .gitignore because the two answer different questions. git is deciding what
# belongs in history; this is deciding what the builder needs to do its job.

.venv/
node_modules/
**/node_modules/
**/.next/
.git/

# Local state and secrets, which must never leave this machine.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
!.env.prod.example
secrets/
.docker-data/

# Test and tooling caches.
.pytest_cache/
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
**/__pycache__/
.hypothesis/
htmlcov/
.coverage
